		{
			dependencies: ["047FECE40CB5A791"]
			description: [
				"{\"text\":\"There is a mission available\",\"italic\":\"true\",\"underlined\":\"true\",\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"3740DE62D42A4D0D\"}}"
				"Can also be synthesized by compressor"
				"Efficient template writing tool"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"How to use: F3+H in advance to display advanced prompt box"
				"If you right-click to open it, you will see a misaligned UI."
				"Here is an example of generating a stamping ingot model:"
				"Check out the recipe for a stamping ingot at JEI."
				"(Here I am looking at iron bars made from iron ingots)"
				"You can see that the item ID of the iron ingot is minecraft:iron_ingot"
				"The iron item ID is gtceu:iron_rod"
				"The recipe ID is gtceu:extruder/extrude_iron_to_rod"
				"Extract recipe ID from stamp: extruder"
				"Programming circuit is: 0 (no programming circuit is 0) Ingot is: ingot Rod is: rod"
				"Fill in the tools in order:"
				"extruder 0 (the multiple model you want) ingot is left blank Rod is left blank"
				"(Remember to click the checkmark to save after filling out. Do not fill in “do not fill in”)"
				"Click to get sample"
				"The tool will automatically search for models in the JEI that meet the conditions and write them automatically (extra models from the backpack will fall to the floor)"
				"&6PS1 It is best not to generate and input samples containing the following items: integrated circuits, electronic circuits, hyperspace circuits, MRI circuits, vacuum tubes, NAND control circuits, processors, because this tool cannot generate a general-purpose circuit board for you. Or use a separate sample set to test and check in the sample management terminal whether any samples use these things."
				"&4PS2: There is no programming circuit in the generated sample input!!!"
				"&aPS3: There may be some recipes that use silica rock from the Stargate mod, but you cannot make silica rock. You can blacklist sgjourney."
				"&2PS4: In fact, the samples obtained in this way will include samples of long rods made from ingots. The tools that really must be completed are the following:"
				"extruder 0 (the multiple model you want) ingot leaves long blank rod"
				"Fill long in output blacklist to filter long pole samples"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Principle: Process the model and record the model input and output data through NBT."
				"Each type of item/recipe in MC has an independent ID"
				"It can be seen showing the advanced prompt box"
				"Many GT recipes have programming circuits for non-consumable items, and the programming circuits are configured through NBT registration numbers."
				"Set Recipe Type: Specify the type of recipe retrieved by the recipe model debug tool (can be seen in JEI by displaying the advanced prompt box and passing if it matches)"
				"Set programming circuit: Specify the programming circuit number of the non-consumable item of this recipe (match means approved, fill in 0 if there is no programming circuit)"
				"The following four functions specify multiple space-separated strings. Don't forget"
				"Enter whitelist ID keyword: Specify the string to include in the input item ID (match one to pass)"
				"Enter blacklist ID keyword: specify the string that cannot be included in the input item ID (if it matches, it will be rejected)"
				"Output Whitelist ID Keyword: Specify the string to be included in the output item ID (the corresponding one will pass)"
				"Output Blacklist ID Keyword: Specify a string that cannot be included in the output item ID (if one matches, it will be rejected)"
			]
			id: "21843C84B76FAD5C"
